{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1541113682","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"5DwvybphxKR6r1cbBeyDx7","dateCreated":"2024-10-18T15:17:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-11-18T22:00:10+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/dynamodb/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon DynamoDB\u003c/a\u003e is a serverless, NoSQL, fully managed database with single-digit millisecond performance at any scale. Today, we are announcing the general availability of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/identity/attribute-based-access-control/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eattribute-based access control (ABAC)\u003c/a\u003e support for tables and indexes in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Commercial Regions\u003c/a\u003e and the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. ABAC is an authorization strategy that lets you define access permissions based on tags attached to users, roles, and AWS resources. Using ABAC with DynamoDB helps you simplify permission management with your tables and indexes as your applications and organizations scale.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nABAC uses tag-based conditions in your AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) policies or other policies to allow or deny specific actions on your tables or indexes when IAM principals\u0026rsquo; tags match the tags for the tables. Using tag-based conditions, you can also set more granular access permissions based on your organizational structures. ABAC automatically applies your tag-based permissions to new employees and changing resource structures, without rewriting policies as organizations grow.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThere is no additional cost to use ABAC. You can get started with ABAC using the AWS Management Console, AWS API, AWS CLI, AWS SDK, or AWS CloudFormation. Learn more at \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/attribute-based-access-control.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUsing attribute-based access control with DynamoDB\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/amazon-dynamodb-general-availability-attribute-based-access-control","postDateTime":"2024-11-18T16:55:00-04:00","contentType":"launch announcement","headline":"Amazon DynamoDB announces general availability of attribute-based access control"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-dynamodb","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-dynamodb","description":"general:products/amazon-dynamodb","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#tag-policies","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"tag-policies","description":"general:products/tag-policies","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:42:11+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-07-aws-organizations-increases-quotas-tag-policies","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/aws-organizations-increases-quotas-tag-policies/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:09:17+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eTag policies help you govern tag consistency across resources in your organization\u0027s accounts. For example, with tag policies, you can define rules on tag keys, including how they should be capitalized and their allowed values. With this release, the maximum size of a tag policy document has been increased from 2.5k to 10k characters for both new and existing tag policies. The number of allowed policies has also been increased from 5 to 10. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith these increased quotas, you can support more tag rules, longer lists of allowed value options, and larger sets of resource types for enforcement. You can now create up to 10 tag policies at the organization root, 10 tag policies in each nested organizational unit up to 5 levels deep, and 10 tag policies in an account. In this nested hierarchy, you will now have a total of up to 70 tag polices with 10k characters each to standardize tags at the account level, an 8x character count increase.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of regions where tag policies are available, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-supported-regions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSupported Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about quotas for tag policies, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_reference_limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eQuotas for AWS Organizations\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTag policies\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS Organizations Developer Guide.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-07-12T16:24:04Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/aws-organizations-increases-quotas-tag-policies/","postDateTime":"2021-07-12T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Organizations increases quotas for tag policies","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eTag policies help you govern tag consistency across resources in your organization\u0027s accounts. For example, with tag policies, you can define rules on tag keys, including how they should be capitalized and their allowed values. With this release, the maximum size of a tag policy document has been increased from 2.5k to 10k characters for both new and existing tag policies. The number of allowed policies has also been increased from 5 to 10. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#tag-policies","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"tag-policies","description":"general:products/tag-policies","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:42:11+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#security-identity-and-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"security-identity-and-compliance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/security-identity-and-compliance","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-tag-policies","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-tag-policies","description":"general:products/aws-tag-policies","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:42:11+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":2,"totalHits":2},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}